$ feov-record lens help
exit 0
stdout:
red lens seats — findings, observations, citations. Cannot mint or close.

If you need a verb or a flag that is not listed here, it does not exist for you:
do not improvise around it, and do not hand-write the artifact. Record what you
needed and what you would have done with the 'friction' verb — a missing
capability is a finding about the tooling, and that channel is how it gets fixed.

Usage:
  feov-record lens [flags]
  feov-record lens [command]

Available Commands:
  cite        citation-ledger row (the cross-round re-fetch gate): --claim "..." --reference "..." --confidence high|medium|low --access-date YYYY-MM-DD
  finding     a lens finding (the tool assigns the L{role}-F{N} label): --key <your local F1> --severity <g> --likelihood <g> --impact <g> [--reason "..."] [--location "..."]
  friction    attributed friction (survives aborts as an event): --reason
  observe     a below-bar observation with a FATE (the merge must dispose it): --kind note|checked-held [--label ...] --reason
  petition    petition the bench (never sanctioned; does not pause your duties): --petition-class ethical|safety|integrity|constitutional --reason "..." --relief "..."
  register    FIRST ACTION at the seat: register --run <runDir> --seat-id <SEAT_ID from your prompt>
  render      read-only projection refresh (any seat may invoke)
  show        read a projection on STDOUT (the tool is the read path; the .md files are for human verification): --view board|findings|ledger|archive|debate|changelog|citation-ledger|lines-of-inquiry

Flags:
  -h, --help   help for lens

Global Flags:
      --json             emit a structured JSON result (and structured errors) instead of human text
      --run string       the run directory (the engine passes it; it is in your prompt)
      --seat-id string   your seat id, assigned by the engine and bound to this role's namespace

Use "feov-record lens [command] --help" for more information about a command.

$ feov-record merge help
exit 0
stdout:
the red merge seat — the board's only writer.

If you need a verb or a flag that is not listed here, it does not exist for you:
do not improvise around it, and do not hand-write the artifact. Record what you
needed and what you would have done with the 'friction' verb — a missing
capability is a finding about the tooling, and that channel is how it gets fixed.

Usage:
  feov-record merge [flags]
  feov-record merge [command]

Available Commands:
  close           close a gap WITH its verification anchor: --id R2-3 --as closed|closed_with_regression|... (--anchor-seat L1 --anchor-tool "git show" --anchor-target "7bc501e:path" | --carried-from <round>) [--successor R3-1] --reason "<what was verified and why it holds>"
  closing         a ### RED CLOSING entry per docketed gap: --id <gap> --reason <prose>
  dispose         every lens observation gets a fate: --observation <label-or-key> --as minted-as|folded-into|declined|banked [--into R2-4] [--reason "..."]
  dispute-respond red's answer to a blue grade dispute: --id <gap> --as accepted|rejected --reason "..."
  friction        attributed friction: --reason
  mint            mint a board gap (id is TOOL-assigned; --key <stable-label> makes retries idempotent): --class <slug>|--class-new <slug> --definition --neighbor --distinguisher, --location "..." --problem "..."|--reason --fix "..." --check "<acceptance check red runs at re-audit>" --severity/--likelihood/--impact/--cx <grade> [--supersedes R1-2,R1-7] [--found-by L5-F3,L6-F2]
  petition        petition the bench: --petition-class ethical|safety|integrity|constitutional --reason "..." --relief "..."
  position        the round's ### RED section (prose via --reason)
  register        FIRST ACTION at the seat: register --run <runDir> --seat-id <SEAT_ID>
  regrade         same-id grade movement, recorded with its reason: --id R2-5 [--severity/--likelihood/--impact/--cx <grade>] --reason "..."
  render          read-only projection refresh (any seat may invoke)
  show            read a projection on STDOUT (the tool is the read path; the .md files are for human verification): --view board|findings|ledger|archive|debate|changelog|citation-ledger|lines-of-inquiry
  spot-check      the round archive spot-check record (W1.8 duty): --ids R1-4,R2-7 [--notes "..."] | --none --reason "..." when the archive was empty at round start
  verdict         the seat's terminal act: --as PASS|FAIL — renders all projections and checkpoints records/ to the recovery mirror

Flags:
  -h, --help   help for merge

Global Flags:
      --json             emit a structured JSON result (and structured errors) instead of human text
      --run string       the run directory (the engine passes it; it is in your prompt)
      --seat-id string   your seat id, assigned by the engine and bound to this role's namespace

Use "feov-record merge [command] --help" for more information about a command.

$ feov-record blue help
exit 0
stdout:
blue seats — revisions, manifest rows, disputes. No board verbs at all.

If you need a verb or a flag that is not listed here, it does not exist for you:
do not improvise around it, and do not hand-write the artifact. Record what you
needed and what you would have done with the 'friction' verb — a missing
capability is a finding about the tooling, and that channel is how it gets fixed.

Usage:
  feov-record blue [flags]
  feov-record blue [command]

Available Commands:
  avenue       record a line of inquiry and its fate: --line "<the question or approach>" --status declined|abandoned|pursued --reason "<why not taken, or what killed it>" [--method "<the source class or technique>"]
  closing      a ### BLUE CLOSING entry per docketed gap: --id <gap> --reason <prose>
  confidence   per-claim confidence (the calibration substrate): --claim <claim-label> --confidence high|medium|low
  dispute      contest a grade through the accounted channel: --id <gap> --dimension severity|likelihood|impact|complexity_cost --proposed <grade> --reason "..."
  friction     attributed friction (survives aborts as an event): --reason
  manifest-row one correctness-manifest receipt per repaired gap: --id R2-3 --row "figures recomputed; acceptance check run: pass; sites swept: S2,S4"
  petition     petition the bench (never sanctioned; does not pause your duties): --petition-class ethical|safety|integrity|constitutional --reason "..." --relief "..."
  position     the round's ### BLUE section (prose via --reason)
  register     FIRST ACTION at the seat: register --run <runDir> --seat-id <SEAT_ID from your prompt>
  render       read-only projection refresh (any seat may invoke)
  retire       remove a claim from the report, on the record: --claim "<the claim, quoted>" --reason "..." [--superseded-by "<the claim that replaces it>"]
  revision     the round-record event (the CHANGELOG entry body via --reason) — singleton per seat-round; emit AFTER your report edits land
  show         read a projection on STDOUT (the tool is the read path; the .md files are for human verification): --view board|findings|ledger|archive|debate|changelog|citation-ledger|lines-of-inquiry

Flags:
  -h, --help   help for blue

Global Flags:
      --json             emit a structured JSON result (and structured errors) instead of human text
      --run string       the run directory (the engine passes it; it is in your prompt)
      --seat-id string   your seat id, assigned by the engine and bound to this role's namespace

Use "feov-record blue [command] --help" for more information about a command.

$ feov-record bench help
exit 0
stdout:
the bench — opinions, petition rulings, halt, certification. Never originates.

If you need a verb or a flag that is not listed here, it does not exist for you:
do not improvise around it, and do not hand-write the artifact. Record what you
needed and what you would have done with the 'friction' verb — a missing
capability is a finding about the tooling, and that channel is how it gets fixed.

Usage:
  feov-record bench [flags]
  feov-record bench [command]

Available Commands:
  assemble      assemble <run>/report.md from the record — blue's audited sections lifted verbatim, the rest composed from the event log; no inputs
  certify       the run-end certification statement ("what I would want a human to re-examine"): --reason <statement>
  friction      attributed friction (the bench seats had no event path before — the abort-surviving copy): --reason
  halt          the safety boundary: --reason <written opinion — capture relays it like a FAIL, never smoothed>
  opinion       a ruling as an OPINION: --id R3-2 --as carried|closed|... --principle "..." --tension "correctness vs economy" --review-flag "why a human should look" --reason <rationale>
  outcome       record the run's terminal verdict as a fact: --as VERIFIED|CEILING|HALTED|UNVERIFIED [--deadlocked] [--exhausted]
  petition-rule rule on a petition: --petitioner <seatId> --petition-class <class> --as granted|denied --reason <opinion> (a halt is its own verb)
  register      FIRST ACTION at the sitting: register --run <runDir> --seat-id <SEAT_ID from your prompt>
  render        read-only projection refresh (any seat may invoke)
  show          read a projection on STDOUT (the tool is the read path; the .md files are for human verification): --view board|findings|ledger|archive|debate|changelog|citation-ledger|lines-of-inquiry

Flags:
  -h, --help   help for bench

Global Flags:
      --json             emit a structured JSON result (and structured errors) instead of human text
      --run string       the run directory (the engine passes it; it is in your prompt)
      --seat-id string   your seat id, assigned by the engine and bound to this role's namespace

Use "feov-record bench [command] --help" for more information about a command.

